+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies a JSON Patch (an array of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`
+and `test` operations, paths being JSON Pointers) and returns the result as a new value; the document and
+the patch are never mutated. It throws `JsonPatchError` when the patch is invalid or an operation fails
+(missing target, bad array index, `move` into a child of `from`, failed `test`); a failing patch has no
+effect (section 5). Removing the whole document (`remove` with path `""`) is rejected.
